# Lab 2 – Tools Used in Machine Learning

## Objective

The objective of this lab was to become familiar with the tools and libraries commonly used in machine learning. This included setting up a development environment, working with Python libraries, exploring a dataset, creating visualizations, and practicing basic data analysis techniques.

## What I Did

In this lab, I learned how to work in Jupyter Notebook and Google Colab while using essential Python libraries such as Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, and Scikit-learn. I loaded the Iris dataset, explored its structure, calculated basic statistics, and created visualizations to better understand the data. I also practiced organizing code and documenting my work using Markdown and GitHub best practices.

## What I Learned

This lab introduced me to the core tools used throughout the machine learning workflow. I learned how to import datasets, inspect and summarize data, create basic charts, and use Python libraries to perform data analysis. I also gained experience with professional documentation and repository organization.

## Skills & Tools

* Python
* Jupyter Notebook
* Google Colab
* Pandas
* NumPy
* Matplotlib
* Scikit-learn
* GitHub
* Markdown

